1
00:00:53,094 --> 00:00:55,597
10:15 on a Saturday night

2
00:00:57,348 --> 00:01:02,270
And the tap drips under the striplight

3
00:01:04,314 --> 00:01:06,816
And I'm sitting in the kitchen sink

4
00:01:09,861 --> 00:01:12,489
And the tap drips
Drip, drip, drip, drip

5
00:01:12,572 --> 00:01:14,699
Drip, drip, drip, drip, drip, drip

6
00:01:41,518 --> 00:01:42,352
D?

7
00:01:42,894 --> 00:01:44,687
When'd you sneak back in?

8
00:01:45,355 --> 00:01:46,481
Hello?

9
00:01:48,650 --> 00:01:49,567
Don't be dead.

10
00:01:52,153 --> 00:01:53,321
Is it morning?

11
00:01:53,947 --> 00:01:54,906
Uh-huh.

12
00:01:56,407 --> 00:01:58,409
But I... The nightmares.

13
00:01:59,410 --> 00:02:01,246
Roman! I didn't dream!

14
00:02:01,329 --> 00:02:03,123
D! Stop it! You're freaking me...

15
00:02:04,666 --> 00:02:06,626
You reek.

16
00:02:08,878 --> 00:02:11,256
'Kay... my ass is clean.

17
00:02:11,339 --> 00:02:12,549
Get my head.

18
00:02:13,758 --> 00:02:15,468
When was your last shower?

19
00:02:15,552 --> 00:02:16,678
Huh...

20
00:02:16,761 --> 00:02:17,971
Lemme see now.

21
00:02:18,054 --> 00:02:20,723
Never mind. Don't answer that.

22
00:02:23,309 --> 00:02:26,437
Most restful morning
I've had in a long while.

23
00:02:26,521 --> 00:02:30,024
So, about yesterday.
It started when you found that shard.

24
00:02:30,525 --> 00:02:31,609
Uh-huh.

25
00:02:31,693 --> 00:02:33,236
Can you still do that stuff?

26
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:34,988
Good question.

27
00:02:40,034 --> 00:02:42,453
Walk. Walk.

28
00:02:42,954 --> 00:02:44,914
Walk. Walk.

29
00:02:44,998 --> 00:02:46,749
- Hey, you were rolling, right?
- Walk.

30
00:02:50,086 --> 00:02:52,505
Yeah, that sure does
look like me, doesn't it?

31
00:02:52,589 --> 00:02:54,549
What do you mean? Course it was you.

32
00:02:55,425 --> 00:02:56,676
- And that girl.
- Huh?

33
00:02:57,427 --> 00:02:58,511
What girl?

34
00:02:58,595 --> 00:03:01,222
Y'know. Bright red, kinda floatin' around?

35
00:03:01,306 --> 00:03:03,725
Bright red? What does that even mean?

36
00:03:03,808 --> 00:03:05,518
Yep. Red as a barn.

37
00:03:05,602 --> 00:03:08,521
Yeah, but what part?
Her hair? Skin? Clothes?

38
00:03:08,605 --> 00:03:10,732
- All of it!
- All of it?

39
00:03:11,232 --> 00:03:14,068
And there were
these glitchy sparky thingies.

40
00:03:14,152 --> 00:03:17,363
A girl that's red all over
with sparky thingies?

41
00:03:18,114 --> 00:03:19,699
Well... that's right.

42
00:03:19,782 --> 00:03:21,284
Cam caught some odd flares.

43
00:03:21,367 --> 00:03:22,911
But the girl?

44
00:03:23,536 --> 00:03:25,205
Choom, she doesn't exist.

45
00:03:25,288 --> 00:03:28,374
She does!
The bitch tried to take over my body!

46
00:03:28,875 --> 00:03:31,878
Sure that shard's
not carryin' a neurovirus?

47
00:03:31,961 --> 00:03:34,297
Should probably yank the thing out. Whoa!

48
00:03:34,380 --> 00:03:37,258
Except viruses are supposed
to weaken systems and slow you down!

49
00:03:37,342 --> 00:03:38,927
The exact opposite of this!

50
00:03:39,010 --> 00:03:40,136
I mean, yeah, I guess.

51
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:43,681
Whatever she did to me, it felt good.

52
00:03:43,765 --> 00:03:45,475
Like I was a kid again.

53
00:03:45,558 --> 00:03:46,893
Like a kid?

54
00:03:48,019 --> 00:03:49,270
Oh, wait, wait, wait!

55
00:03:49,771 --> 00:03:50,647
What is it?

56
00:03:50,730 --> 00:03:52,482
Ugh, the glare.

57
00:03:52,565 --> 00:03:54,651
You looked so happy here, too.

58
00:03:55,443 --> 00:03:58,238
- I was happy?
- Mmm. Dang it.

59
00:04:01,574 --> 00:04:03,368
- D.
- Mmm?

60
00:04:03,910 --> 00:04:06,537
- You gotta yank the shard.
- No way! Why should I?

61
00:04:06,621 --> 00:04:08,039
It's all kinds of bad news!

62
00:04:08,122 --> 00:04:09,958
What more reason do you need?

63
00:04:10,041 --> 00:04:11,793
Said yourself it tried to hijack you.

64
00:04:11,876 --> 00:04:13,419
And you just said I was happy!

65
00:04:13,503 --> 00:04:16,547
So what if you were?
Doesn't mean that thing is safe.

66
00:04:19,550 --> 00:04:23,304
- It's her!
- Hey, now! Don't "her" me, buddy!

67
00:04:23,388 --> 00:04:25,974
Just call me Capri!

68
00:04:26,057 --> 00:04:28,977
Wait. Me? Us? He?

69
00:04:29,060 --> 00:04:30,728
- She? They? We?
- D?

70
00:04:30,812 --> 00:04:32,230
Eh, whatever!

71
00:04:32,313 --> 00:04:34,899
Are you saying she's here? The red girl?

72
00:04:34,983 --> 00:04:37,568
Oh? It's the baby from yesterday!

73
00:04:37,652 --> 00:04:39,112
Hi, little baby!

74
00:04:39,195 --> 00:04:40,530
She's saying hi.

75
00:04:40,613 --> 00:04:42,490
Uh, hi.

76
00:04:42,573 --> 00:04:43,700
What a sweetie-pie.

77
00:04:43,783 --> 00:04:45,243
- You hear that?
- Not a thing.

78
00:04:45,326 --> 00:04:46,494
Or you see that?

79
00:04:46,577 --> 00:04:47,787
Nope.

80
00:04:48,579 --> 00:04:52,500
Nobody can hear me,
nobody can see me. Nobody besides you.

81
00:04:52,583 --> 00:04:54,585
Just what the hell are you, exactly?

82
00:04:54,669 --> 00:04:56,337
What does that matter?

83
00:04:56,421 --> 00:04:58,673
C'mon, let's be friends.

84
00:04:58,756 --> 00:05:01,092
- Gah! Fuck off!
- Hmm.

85
00:05:01,175 --> 00:05:03,720
Friends don't try to hijack
each other's bodies!

86
00:05:03,803 --> 00:05:06,472
- Why? Is that bad?
- Yes!

87
00:05:06,556 --> 00:05:10,226
Just 'cause I tried
doesn't mean I actually did.

88
00:05:10,810 --> 00:05:11,728
Not yet.

89
00:05:12,312 --> 00:05:13,229
Not yet?

90
00:05:13,313 --> 00:05:16,858
Naw, c'mon! Yesterday was so much fun!

91
00:05:16,941 --> 00:05:19,235
- I know you thought so too!
- No, I didn't!

92
00:05:19,319 --> 00:05:21,446
Who are you tryna haze?

93
00:05:21,529 --> 00:05:24,866
We're sharing the same
pink and squishy CPU.

94
00:05:24,949 --> 00:05:27,493
I know if I was havin' a total blast,

95
00:05:27,577 --> 00:05:29,620
it means you had to be, too.

96
00:05:29,704 --> 00:05:31,622
What the hell are you?

97
00:05:31,706 --> 00:05:33,374
Me? I'm Capri.

98
00:05:33,458 --> 00:05:34,917
That's not what I asked.

99
00:05:35,001 --> 00:05:37,795
Oh, you mean, what the hell am I?

100
00:05:37,879 --> 00:05:39,255
Jesus Chr... Ugh.

101
00:05:39,339 --> 00:05:40,923
Isn't that what I just said?

102
00:05:41,007 --> 00:05:42,884
Oh! Wait a minute!

103
00:05:42,967 --> 00:05:43,801
Huh?

104
00:05:43,885 --> 00:05:46,012
Even if I can't see her, that's fine.

105
00:05:46,095 --> 00:05:48,139
But maybe we can patch
her voice through?

106
00:05:49,766 --> 00:05:50,975
Huh?

107
00:05:53,311 --> 00:05:55,313
- Hmm?
- Hah-hah! Hah!

108
00:05:57,732 --> 00:05:58,566
Whoa!

109
00:06:00,902 --> 00:06:04,322
All right. I'm a personality construct.

110
00:06:04,906 --> 00:06:06,199
A construct?

111
00:06:06,282 --> 00:06:08,951
In my case,
a collection of human psyches.

112
00:06:09,035 --> 00:06:12,830
All of them digitized
and rolled into one beautiful me.

113
00:06:12,914 --> 00:06:14,749
So you're an AI?

114
00:06:14,832 --> 00:06:16,459
Are all mammals dogs?

115
00:06:16,542 --> 00:06:19,587
No. AIs got too powerful.
Outgrew the leash.

116
00:06:19,670 --> 00:06:22,465
But their corporate masters
still wanted that power.

117
00:06:22,548 --> 00:06:26,677
So they created me.
Powerful, like an AI, but born of humans.

118
00:06:26,761 --> 00:06:29,055
So very many humans!

119
00:06:29,138 --> 00:06:32,600
You're a weapon?
A weapon made out of people?

120
00:06:33,184 --> 00:06:35,353
Eh. Close enough.

121
00:06:35,436 --> 00:06:38,606
A force the likes of which
the world has never seen!

122
00:06:38,689 --> 00:06:42,360
The trick was finding the right
Joe Schmo or Jane Schlane to stick me in.

123
00:06:42,443 --> 00:06:44,404
You need a human host to run?

124
00:06:44,487 --> 00:06:47,281
Uh-huh! After all,
what good is an operating system

125
00:06:47,365 --> 00:06:49,117
without a computer to operate?

126
00:06:49,826 --> 00:06:51,869
And I was compatible.

127
00:06:51,953 --> 00:06:53,454
Sure looks that way.

128
00:06:53,538 --> 00:06:54,914
Lemme get this straight.

129
00:06:54,997 --> 00:06:58,042
If you'd been successful takin' over
after landin' in my head,

130
00:06:58,126 --> 00:07:00,044
I would've been overwritten, right?

131
00:07:00,128 --> 00:07:01,879
But the install failed somehow.

132
00:07:01,963 --> 00:07:04,799
It's incomplete,
leaving you anchored to this chip.

133
00:07:04,882 --> 00:07:08,761
So, if I yank it,
you get sucked back into your cage?

134
00:07:08,845 --> 00:07:09,929
Mm-hmm.

135
00:07:10,430 --> 00:07:11,514
- Relax.
- Huh?

136
00:07:11,597 --> 00:07:14,016
I'm willing to let you ride shotgun.

137
00:07:14,100 --> 00:07:17,520
But in return, you're gonna share
that power of yours with me.

138
00:07:17,603 --> 00:07:20,022
Assumin' you're not outta tricks.

139
00:07:24,402 --> 00:07:26,028
Her prognosis is clear.

140
00:07:26,112 --> 00:07:29,115
Continued heavy use
and implantation of cyberware

141
00:07:29,198 --> 00:07:32,660
places your daughter
at high risk of acute cyberpsychosis.

142
00:07:32,743 --> 00:07:36,539
We were led to believe that
Talia possesses exceptional tolerance.

143
00:07:36,622 --> 00:07:40,585
The fact that she's remained
stable thus far is exceptional in itself.

144
00:07:40,668 --> 00:07:43,671
Just days ago, you saw no early markers.

145
00:07:43,754 --> 00:07:47,425
Symptoms can be subtle,
heterogenous across individuals,

146
00:07:47,508 --> 00:07:49,218
or even absent altogether.

147
00:07:49,302 --> 00:07:52,430
The pool of diagnostic data
for this disease is limited.

148
00:07:52,513 --> 00:07:55,099
But due to the severity
of Talia 's symptoms,

149
00:07:55,183 --> 00:07:59,187
we were able to confirm her diagnosis
prior to any onset of psychosis.

150
00:07:59,270 --> 00:08:02,398
She's a valuable specimen
for future study.

151
00:08:02,482 --> 00:08:04,150
Specimen?

152
00:08:04,233 --> 00:08:05,693
- Sorry?
- Nothing.

153
00:08:06,319 --> 00:08:08,738
Please send me a full report
of your findings.

154
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:12,241
I'd also like second and third opinions.

155
00:08:12,325 --> 00:08:14,243
Oh. Of course.

156
00:08:14,994 --> 00:08:18,664
By the way,
why are you still hangin' around?

157
00:08:18,748 --> 00:08:20,374
D. Seriously?

158
00:08:20,458 --> 00:08:22,210
You don't gotta tag along anymore.

159
00:08:22,293 --> 00:08:25,421
What? You drag me back and forth,
all over the city,

160
00:08:25,505 --> 00:08:28,591
and then you ditch me the moment
you slot a new choom into your head?

161
00:08:28,674 --> 00:08:31,469
As I recall, your sole aim was
to scroll Maelstrom.

162
00:08:31,552 --> 00:08:32,929
That was just biz.

163
00:08:33,513 --> 00:08:35,932
What I really want is to film you, D.

164
00:08:36,015 --> 00:08:37,808
Me? Why?

165
00:08:37,892 --> 00:08:40,311
Got this feeling
you'll leap off the screen.

166
00:08:40,394 --> 00:08:42,063
The hell's that even mean?

167
00:08:42,730 --> 00:08:45,942
Anyway, can't stroll into Arasaka
with a kid.

168
00:08:46,025 --> 00:08:48,569
Says the guy
clearly scared of goin' himself.

169
00:08:48,653 --> 00:08:51,072
I am not. Smart-ass.

170
00:08:51,656 --> 00:08:54,408
If your stupid butt can get in, so can I.

171
00:09:06,170 --> 00:09:07,797
Whoa.

172
00:09:15,054 --> 00:09:16,055
Which way?

173
00:09:16,973 --> 00:09:18,015
Follow me.

174
00:09:23,062 --> 00:09:25,523
It's like we really are invisible.

175
00:09:26,857 --> 00:09:29,193
Mighty nifty system breach.

176
00:09:31,237 --> 00:09:32,613
Nicely done.

177
00:09:35,324 --> 00:09:39,328
She says there's only a single soul
in Data Archive B right now.

178
00:09:43,958 --> 00:09:45,001
Hmm?

179
00:09:46,085 --> 00:09:47,169
You there!

180
00:09:47,837 --> 00:09:49,422
This is a restricted are--

181
00:09:50,089 --> 00:09:52,133
Mind answering me a few questions?

182
00:09:52,216 --> 00:09:54,552
I do and I won't. This is my office.

183
00:09:54,635 --> 00:09:56,887
Not whatever gutter you crawled out from.

184
00:09:56,971 --> 00:09:58,514
What are you doing, boy?

185
00:09:58,598 --> 00:09:59,807
Filming.

186
00:09:59,890 --> 00:10:01,267
On corporate property?

187
00:10:01,350 --> 00:10:03,394
- Child or not, there are consequ--
- Two years ago.

188
00:10:03,477 --> 00:10:06,689
Saka and Maelstrom.
They hit one of Snake Nation's clans.

189
00:10:06,772 --> 00:10:08,399
and burned the whole camp to ashes.

190
00:10:08,482 --> 00:10:11,152
Who was pulling the strings?

191
00:10:11,235 --> 00:10:12,486
Are you...

192
00:10:12,987 --> 00:10:14,655
Wait a sec. Do you fuckin' know me?

193
00:10:14,739 --> 00:10:16,741
I said no such thing.

194
00:10:17,658 --> 00:10:20,244
Yeah, whatever.
Just gimme all the files on it.

195
00:10:20,328 --> 00:10:21,203
I will not.

196
00:10:21,287 --> 00:10:23,331
I'm this close to blowin'
your fuckin' head clean off.

197
00:10:23,414 --> 00:10:26,459
So do it. If you have the nerve.

198
00:10:31,047 --> 00:10:32,923
Gimme the damn files!

199
00:10:34,884 --> 00:10:35,760
As I thought!

200
00:10:35,843 --> 00:10:37,219
The hell's so funny?

201
00:10:37,303 --> 00:10:39,388
Petty netrunner thief.

202
00:10:39,472 --> 00:10:42,475
You lack conviction to pull the trigger.

203
00:10:45,061 --> 00:10:47,188
The files!

204
00:10:47,271 --> 00:10:50,775
I... refuse.

205
00:10:50,858 --> 00:10:52,985
- Okay! My turn.
- Huh?

206
00:10:55,029 --> 00:10:56,405
Aah!

207
00:10:56,489 --> 00:10:57,948
Couldn't have led with that?

208
00:10:58,032 --> 00:11:00,242
How? That's not possible.

209
00:11:03,871 --> 00:11:05,247
Grab a few winks.

210
00:11:05,331 --> 00:11:07,083
You gotta go easy on him, D.

211
00:11:07,667 --> 00:11:09,293
What if he has Trauma Team?

212
00:11:09,794 --> 00:11:11,295
I did go easy.

213
00:11:11,796 --> 00:11:13,506
He'll wake up in--

214
00:11:15,925 --> 00:11:17,551
Close that right now.

215
00:11:17,635 --> 00:11:19,136
The still? Sure.

216
00:11:20,596 --> 00:11:23,140
What I need's a full list of names.

217
00:11:23,224 --> 00:11:25,142
- No can do.
- Why?

218
00:11:25,226 --> 00:11:27,061
'Cause it doesn't exist.

219
00:11:27,144 --> 00:11:28,312
Can't be right.

220
00:11:28,396 --> 00:11:30,064
So what's the next best thing?

221
00:11:30,147 --> 00:11:32,983
I don't know. It looks like
they scarfed the juicy bites already.

222
00:11:33,067 --> 00:11:34,694
They cleaned house.

223
00:11:34,777 --> 00:11:36,070
There's gotta be somethin'.

224
00:11:36,153 --> 00:11:40,574
Well, might be traces of some lazy deletes
that I could try to undelete.

225
00:11:40,658 --> 00:11:41,784
Get on it, then.

226
00:11:41,867 --> 00:11:43,035
Yessir!

227
00:11:47,498 --> 00:11:50,042
- David Martinez.
- Huh?

228
00:11:50,126 --> 00:11:52,044
That's him, right?

229
00:11:53,713 --> 00:11:55,339
What the hell is this?

230
00:11:55,423 --> 00:11:58,300
David... Martinez.

231
00:11:58,384 --> 00:12:01,220
Rotten edgerunner piece of trash.

232
00:12:01,303 --> 00:12:06,934
How pathetic to think a gang of gutter
rats could push Arasaka to its limits.

233
00:12:07,017 --> 00:12:11,772
And now security can't even stop children
from strolling in off the curb.

234
00:12:11,856 --> 00:12:13,816
What a joke we--

235
00:12:13,899 --> 00:12:16,402
I know you know names.
So gimme the biggest.

236
00:12:16,485 --> 00:12:18,696
- Beats me.
- Bullshit!

237
00:12:19,989 --> 00:12:23,701
You recognized me earlier. Didn't you?

238
00:12:23,784 --> 00:12:26,829
[man Oh, please. You're nobody.

239
00:12:26,912 --> 00:12:30,082
Nobodies don't have
their faces in classified files.

240
00:12:31,167 --> 00:12:32,752
What's the point?

241
00:12:33,252 --> 00:12:35,588
They shuttered the project.

242
00:12:35,671 --> 00:12:38,424
Project? What project?

243
00:12:38,507 --> 00:12:40,134
You're wasting your time.

244
00:12:40,217 --> 00:12:42,303
The truth will always evade you.

245
00:12:42,386 --> 00:12:44,054
Fuck that!

246
00:12:44,138 --> 00:12:46,849
You came here looking for blood,
didn't you?

247
00:12:50,019 --> 00:12:51,353
Why're you laughing?

248
00:12:51,437 --> 00:12:53,355
- Huh?
- Because it tickles me.

249
00:12:53,439 --> 00:12:57,485
This vengeance you sorely seek
but will never find.

250
00:12:57,568 --> 00:12:58,778
Speak plainly!

251
00:12:58,861 --> 00:13:00,321
You gnawed your way in

252
00:13:00,404 --> 00:13:04,575
believing a lone termite could topple
the mighty house of Arasaka.

253
00:13:04,658 --> 00:13:08,913
But that belief will kill you,
the same as it killed Martinez.

254
00:13:08,996 --> 00:13:12,875
The insignificant die
as the insignificant deserve.

255
00:13:12,958 --> 00:13:15,169
Maybe. But I can take you with me.

256
00:13:15,252 --> 00:13:16,378
Huh?

257
00:13:16,462 --> 00:13:17,797
Then do it!

258
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:20,382
My career won't survive the day anyway.

259
00:13:22,009 --> 00:13:24,345
D! You'll call Trauma!

260
00:13:30,476 --> 00:13:32,520
Still breathin'.

261
00:13:32,603 --> 00:13:35,564
But I bet that tripped an alert.
We gotta go.

262
00:13:35,648 --> 00:13:36,524
Run away?

263
00:13:36,607 --> 00:13:40,402
Unless you wanna scrap it out with TT
on Arasaka turf, we gotta move!

264
00:13:40,486 --> 00:13:42,404
Fuck.

265
00:13:45,950 --> 00:13:47,409
Huh?

266
00:13:47,910 --> 00:13:48,786
Hmm?

267
00:13:49,495 --> 00:13:50,496
Talia?

268
00:13:51,497 --> 00:13:53,290
- C'mon!
- Right.

269
00:14:01,257 --> 00:14:04,552
How are things?
How's your daughter Talia?

270
00:14:04,635 --> 00:14:08,556
Doing well. Aside from a bad case
of teenage rebellion, of course.

271
00:14:08,639 --> 00:14:10,933
She is at that age, isn't she?

272
00:14:11,016 --> 00:14:12,184
Yes.

273
00:14:12,268 --> 00:14:14,937
She's had more implants installed, I hear.

274
00:14:15,020 --> 00:14:17,606
Yes, but she's adapting well.

275
00:14:17,690 --> 00:14:18,691
Is that so?

276
00:14:18,774 --> 00:14:21,151
According to the report I received,

277
00:14:21,235 --> 00:14:24,530
another surgery could cause
a full psychotic break.

278
00:14:24,613 --> 00:14:26,949
No, sir. That's an exaggeration.

279
00:14:27,032 --> 00:14:29,451
The incident has been blown
way out of proportion.

280
00:14:29,535 --> 00:14:31,704
She's been otherwise stable.

281
00:14:32,288 --> 00:14:34,748
Then why neglect to report it yourself?

282
00:14:35,291 --> 00:14:37,251
Secrets rot trust, Kiril.

283
00:14:37,334 --> 00:14:40,212
Trust already damaged
by your loss of the chip.

284
00:14:40,296 --> 00:14:42,840
Yes, sir. I apologize again for that.

285
00:14:42,923 --> 00:14:46,218
The mercenary I hired
had come highly recommended.

286
00:14:46,302 --> 00:14:48,429
You hired a goon from the streets.

287
00:14:48,512 --> 00:14:51,432
In any case,
it's Arasaka that vexes me now.

288
00:14:51,515 --> 00:14:53,100
They aren't scrambling.

289
00:14:53,183 --> 00:14:56,854
They've scarcely mobilized
to retrieve this prized chip of theirs.

290
00:14:56,937 --> 00:15:00,316
In fact, I hear
they intend to abandon it entirely.

291
00:15:00,399 --> 00:15:03,944
I suspect that's a bluff
to create this very kind of doubt.

292
00:15:04,028 --> 00:15:06,864
Maybe. But Arasaka can no longer afford

293
00:15:06,947 --> 00:15:09,825
the luxury of nuance and clever ploys.

294
00:15:09,909 --> 00:15:12,077
Their house is cracking
at its foundations.

295
00:15:12,161 --> 00:15:14,872
Their stranglehold on the city has broken.

296
00:15:14,955 --> 00:15:16,415
That is undeniable.

297
00:15:16,498 --> 00:15:17,625
True.

298
00:15:17,708 --> 00:15:20,085
With Arasaka's influence
already on the wane,

299
00:15:20,169 --> 00:15:23,964
leadership is losing interest
in seizing the project outright.

300
00:15:24,048 --> 00:15:27,092
Should the chip fall into our laps, fantastic.

301
00:15:27,176 --> 00:15:31,597
Should it get dragged down and buried
beneath the sinking ship of Arasaka,

302
00:15:31,680 --> 00:15:33,265
that too is acceptable.

303
00:15:33,349 --> 00:15:36,518
No matter the outcome,
Kang Tao stands to win.

304
00:15:36,602 --> 00:15:37,603
I understand.

305
00:15:37,686 --> 00:15:39,271
That being said, Kiril,

306
00:15:39,355 --> 00:15:42,441
you owe your standing
in the company to this initiative.

307
00:15:42,524 --> 00:15:43,609
Yes, sir.

308
00:15:43,692 --> 00:15:46,111
So squeeze it for all it's worth.

309
00:15:46,612 --> 00:15:48,781
There are still victories to be won here.

310
00:15:48,864 --> 00:15:51,742
Prove I was right to see potential in you.

311
00:15:52,326 --> 00:15:53,619
You have my word.

312
00:15:54,203 --> 00:15:58,248
Well, then, the next time we meet,
I'll expect to see results as promised.

313
00:15:58,874 --> 00:16:00,125
You'll have them, sir.

314
00:16:06,757 --> 00:16:07,633
Weak!

315
00:16:08,217 --> 00:16:09,760
She okay? Talia?

316
00:16:09,843 --> 00:16:13,764
I told the hospital to keep
a close watch on her. I was clear.

317
00:16:13,847 --> 00:16:17,726
She ran off? Knowing she might pop...
go psycho any minute?

318
00:16:18,978 --> 00:16:20,521
You haven't told her yet?

319
00:16:20,604 --> 00:16:22,147
Someone's gotta talk to her.

320
00:16:22,231 --> 00:16:23,774
Don't you do it! Not yet.

321
00:16:23,857 --> 00:16:26,360
You put that thought in her head,
get her worrying about it,

322
00:16:26,443 --> 00:16:28,195
could be what sets the girl off.

323
00:16:28,278 --> 00:16:30,280
What ifs, what ifs. Can't worry about 'em.

324
00:16:30,364 --> 00:16:31,281
Course I can!

325
00:16:31,365 --> 00:16:34,535
We got no idea what might
cause another episode. Or worse!

326
00:16:34,618 --> 00:16:36,704
You don't understand how fragile she is!

327
00:16:36,787 --> 00:16:38,455
Well, uh... I do, I do.

328
00:16:38,539 --> 00:16:41,875
- Then don't talk like that!
- Right, right. Wasn't thinkin'.

329
00:16:41,959 --> 00:16:43,544
Better get movin'. Gotta go.

330
00:16:43,627 --> 00:16:45,087
Gonna get her home to you soon.

331
00:16:45,170 --> 00:16:48,549
Please hurry, Weak.
What if those gang freaks have her?

332
00:16:49,216 --> 00:16:52,428
Yeah... Not too worried about that.

333
00:17:02,688 --> 00:17:04,231
Thought I'd find you here.

334
00:17:04,732 --> 00:17:06,608
Looks like they ditched ya.

335
00:17:08,027 --> 00:17:09,820
And sounds like you blame me.

336
00:17:10,362 --> 00:17:12,072
They're prob'ly just fuckin' around.

337
00:17:12,156 --> 00:17:16,952
C'mon. You don't buy into their cult
bullshit, so why risk your life?

338
00:17:17,036 --> 00:17:18,787
Talking like you know me.

339
00:17:19,288 --> 00:17:21,415
They're pretty touchy about outsiders.

340
00:17:21,498 --> 00:17:23,917
- Prob'ly saw right through ya.
- The hell do you know--

341
00:17:24,001 --> 00:17:27,504
'Sall right. I know you don't chip
all that chrome out of love for it.

342
00:17:27,588 --> 00:17:29,798
That for you, it's a matter of survival.

343
00:17:31,175 --> 00:17:34,720
Sorry. Your mom told me about it.
Your condition.

344
00:17:34,803 --> 00:17:36,180
Okay. So?

345
00:17:36,847 --> 00:17:38,432
Come on. Let's grab a tight bite.

346
00:17:38,515 --> 00:17:39,683
What?

347
00:17:39,767 --> 00:17:41,810
Shoot the shit over some SCOP dogs.

348
00:17:41,894 --> 00:17:43,812
And why the hell would I do that?

349
00:17:43,896 --> 00:17:47,232
So I don't drag your ass
back to the hospital.

350
00:17:47,316 --> 00:17:48,901
Leave the choice to you.

351
00:17:52,321 --> 00:17:56,075
Hey. Heard you went psycho. That true?

352
00:17:56,158 --> 00:17:58,077
It is.

353
00:17:58,160 --> 00:18:02,581
And you're the one to lecture me
on healthy chippin' habits? That's rich.

354
00:18:02,664 --> 00:18:05,334
No one more qualified,
for just that reason.

355
00:18:08,170 --> 00:18:10,506
Got more in common than ya think.

356
00:18:10,589 --> 00:18:13,258
Know exactly what's been
goin' through your mind.

357
00:18:13,342 --> 00:18:15,594
That's almost funny.

358
00:18:15,677 --> 00:18:17,346
We have nothing in common.

359
00:18:17,930 --> 00:18:21,141
Lemme guess, you think
you've got a high tolerance for chrome.

360
00:18:21,225 --> 00:18:23,393
That you're different. Special.

361
00:18:23,477 --> 00:18:26,105
More you chip, the more you feel like you.

362
00:18:26,188 --> 00:18:27,439
So did I.

363
00:18:27,523 --> 00:18:29,650
Except look how you turned out.

364
00:18:29,733 --> 00:18:33,320
That's my point.
You're not special. No one is.

365
00:18:33,403 --> 00:18:34,863
You're wrong.

366
00:18:34,947 --> 00:18:36,907
A lot of people have thought that.

367
00:18:36,990 --> 00:18:38,867
Believed they were just wired different.

368
00:18:38,951 --> 00:18:42,371
But every single one of 'em
either went spiralin' over the edge

369
00:18:42,454 --> 00:18:44,915
or flatlined before they had the chance.

370
00:18:44,998 --> 00:18:48,377
Sooner or later. Just a matter of time.

371
00:18:48,460 --> 00:18:49,753
What am I supposed to do?

372
00:18:49,837 --> 00:18:52,464
Hold on to the last ganic bits I got left?

373
00:18:52,548 --> 00:18:54,299
Fragile and failing?

374
00:18:54,383 --> 00:18:57,052
Chrome's the only thing
still giving me any hope.

375
00:18:57,136 --> 00:18:59,555
You don't know if I'll go psycho.
You can't know.

376
00:18:59,638 --> 00:19:01,682
But if I stop now, I'm dead for sure!

377
00:19:01,765 --> 00:19:04,768
Really expect me
to just curl up and croak?

378
00:19:05,352 --> 00:19:07,479
Oh! Whoa. Uh...

379
00:19:10,566 --> 00:19:13,026
Yeah, so maybe I do go psycho.

380
00:19:13,110 --> 00:19:16,238
Maybe. But even that's better
than definitely dying.

381
00:19:16,321 --> 00:19:17,739
No! It's not!

382
00:19:17,823 --> 00:19:19,116
Not at all.

383
00:19:19,199 --> 00:19:23,203
Most just think of the violence.
The tics, the rage, the outbursts.

384
00:19:23,287 --> 00:19:25,497
But what's worse is you stop being you.

385
00:19:26,123 --> 00:19:27,499
Losing yourself...

386
00:19:27,583 --> 00:19:29,501
That's worse than death.

387
00:19:31,336 --> 00:19:32,754
So what are you saying?

388
00:19:32,838 --> 00:19:35,757
Better I die now? Get it over with?

389
00:19:35,841 --> 00:19:37,509
No. Course not.

390
00:19:38,093 --> 00:19:40,512
But to go through that...

391
00:19:40,596 --> 00:19:43,849
Friends, family. No one's really safe.

392
00:19:43,932 --> 00:19:46,643
Could kill somebody you love
and not remember it.

393
00:19:46,727 --> 00:19:48,270
Not know why.

394
00:19:49,688 --> 00:19:50,981
Did you?

395
00:19:51,064 --> 00:19:52,399
I don't know.

396
00:19:52,482 --> 00:19:53,734
You don't know?

397
00:19:53,817 --> 00:19:56,028
That's what I'm sayin'. It's a blur.

398
00:19:56,111 --> 00:19:57,905
Faces, places, time.

399
00:19:57,988 --> 00:20:01,283
You dont know when
or where you are anymore.

400
00:20:01,366 --> 00:20:03,118
Don't know who you are.

401
00:20:03,202 --> 00:20:05,370
Like, you see old memories?

402
00:20:05,454 --> 00:20:06,496
Uh...

403
00:20:07,039 --> 00:20:08,040
That's rough.

404
00:20:10,626 --> 00:20:13,629
So, if there's a chance
I might hurt someone,

405
00:20:13,712 --> 00:20:16,423
I should prob'ly stay away
from my parents, yeah?

406
00:20:16,506 --> 00:20:18,926
You mean run away and live on your own?

407
00:20:19,009 --> 00:20:21,136
Pretty childish idea, don't ya think?

408
00:20:21,220 --> 00:20:22,471
- You're one to talk.
- Uh...

409
00:20:22,554 --> 00:20:25,015
- Bet you live alone.
- Well, that's different.

410
00:20:25,098 --> 00:20:27,559
Uh-huh. Why're you so involved, anyway?

411
00:20:27,643 --> 00:20:29,519
'Cause my mom asked nicely?

412
00:20:29,603 --> 00:20:31,271
Or, don't tell me.

413
00:20:31,355 --> 00:20:32,606
An affair?

414
00:20:32,689 --> 00:20:34,483
How dare you talk
about your mother that way?

415
00:20:34,566 --> 00:20:37,778
She's a good woman!
She'd never do something like that.

416
00:20:37,861 --> 00:20:39,988
All you need to know is
the two of us go way back,

417
00:20:40,072 --> 00:20:41,490
and she's very special to me.

418
00:20:41,573 --> 00:20:43,909
But, like, romantically? Or...

419
00:20:43,992 --> 00:20:46,703
C'mon! What the hell
are you grillin' my ass for?

420
00:20:46,787 --> 00:20:48,664
The relationship that we have...

421
00:20:48,747 --> 00:20:50,123
Mmm...

422
00:20:50,207 --> 00:20:52,709
Well, it's kinda hard to explain to a kid.

423
00:20:53,919 --> 00:20:56,672
I'm serious. Some things
you learn with age.

424
00:20:56,755 --> 00:20:58,632
Maturity comes with experience.

425
00:20:58,715 --> 00:21:00,425
- Uh...
- Maturity, huh?

426
00:21:00,926 --> 00:21:03,845
Been hung up on
the same woman for, what, decades?

427
00:21:03,929 --> 00:21:05,514
And never moved on?

428
00:21:05,597 --> 00:21:07,933
That's not maturity. That's pathetic.

429
00:21:10,435 --> 00:21:12,813
Uh...

430
00:21:13,689 --> 00:21:15,774
You really gonna critique my love life?

431
00:21:15,857 --> 00:21:17,818
If you had one, I would.

432
00:21:18,318 --> 00:21:21,405
Think you know love
from readin' teen magazines?

433
00:21:21,488 --> 00:21:24,408
- 'Scuse me?
- Sure like to talk a big game, don'tcha?

434
00:21:24,491 --> 00:21:26,576
For someone who hasn't
moved past hand-holdin'.

435
00:21:26,660 --> 00:21:29,288
- You tryna die?
- Hey, it's not your fault--

436
00:21:32,040 --> 00:21:33,292
Uh... Ohh.

437
00:21:33,375 --> 00:21:34,418
I'm callin' him.

438
00:21:34,501 --> 00:21:36,253
- Huh?
- My boyfriend.

439
00:21:36,837 --> 00:21:39,256
Wanna meet him? I'll call him right now.

440
00:21:39,339 --> 00:21:41,300
Whoa. Wait!

441
00:21:47,764 --> 00:21:49,558
- You lookin' for somethin'?
- Hmm?

442
00:21:50,225 --> 00:21:52,394
If it's clouds, I think you're in luck.

443
00:21:56,315 --> 00:21:58,650
- Satellites?
- Huh?

444
00:21:58,734 --> 00:22:00,277
Why satellites?

445
00:22:03,196 --> 00:22:04,614
The hell's so funny?

446
00:22:06,408 --> 00:22:08,869
Shoulda kept a cooler head, D.

447
00:22:08,952 --> 00:22:10,120
Hmm.

448
00:22:10,203 --> 00:22:11,955
I get how you feel, but...

449
00:22:12,039 --> 00:22:13,915
Look who's gettin' lectured by a baby!

450
00:22:13,999 --> 00:22:15,167
Shut up.

451
00:22:15,751 --> 00:22:17,252
Was that aimed at me, or...

452
00:22:17,336 --> 00:22:18,628
Capri.

453
00:22:18,712 --> 00:22:20,047
That's the girl?

454
00:22:20,130 --> 00:22:21,923
She says that's her name.

455
00:22:22,007 --> 00:22:23,592
Capri, huh?

456
00:22:23,675 --> 00:22:25,218
Nice to meet ya, Capri.

457
00:22:25,302 --> 00:22:26,678
Little to the right.

458
00:22:28,388 --> 00:22:30,640
And there's really no way I can see her?

459
00:22:31,266 --> 00:22:32,893
Maybe a flash?

460
00:22:34,269 --> 00:22:35,812
I think I saw somethin'.

461
00:22:35,896 --> 00:22:37,689
Let's see. Check it.

462
00:22:40,275 --> 00:22:41,193
Whoa!

463
00:22:41,276 --> 00:22:42,986
Yeah, that's her!

464
00:22:43,779 --> 00:22:46,448
It's like one of those paranormal shows.

465
00:22:46,531 --> 00:22:48,450
No ghost is that goofy-lookin'?

466
00:22:48,533 --> 00:22:49,993
I think I look spooky.

467
00:22:51,161 --> 00:22:52,704
- Hmm?
- Huh? Talia?

468
00:22:57,793 --> 00:22:58,710
Uh, now?

469
00:22:58,794 --> 00:23:00,045
Please and thanks.

470
00:23:00,128 --> 00:23:02,130
Gah!

471
00:23:02,214 --> 00:23:04,674
Really let your friend
push you around like that?

472
00:23:04,758 --> 00:23:06,593
- Like you're one to talk.
- Oooh!

473
00:23:07,135 --> 00:23:08,512
Wait...

474
00:23:08,595 --> 00:23:10,222
Hey! You snooped!

475
00:23:10,305 --> 00:23:12,933
Ugh! Not cool, choom.

476
00:23:14,267 --> 00:23:16,061
So, do you wanna come along?

477
00:23:16,144 --> 00:23:18,480
I'll pass. She sounds scary.

478
00:23:18,980 --> 00:23:21,691
You know, she was on that list too.

479
00:23:21,775 --> 00:23:23,360
With you and David Martinez.

480
00:23:23,443 --> 00:23:24,486
- What?
- Huh?

481
00:23:24,569 --> 00:23:28,949
Even if we don't understand what
it means, you're all connected somehow.

482
00:23:29,032 --> 00:23:30,909
What we're missin', she might know.

483
00:23:31,410 --> 00:23:34,162
Martinez and I have fuck all in common.

484
00:23:34,246 --> 00:23:36,081
Then why are you on the same list?

485
00:23:36,665 --> 00:23:38,500
There has to be a reason.

486
00:23:38,583 --> 00:23:39,709
Hmph.

487
00:23:40,335 --> 00:23:42,087
'Kay, I'll go alone.

488
00:23:43,171 --> 00:23:45,006
Your dead end just found new life.

489
00:23:45,882 --> 00:23:47,509
Why stop now?

490
00:23:48,343 --> 00:23:49,344
Fine.

491
00:23:49,970 --> 00:23:51,179
I'll join ya.

492
00:23:52,431 --> 00:23:53,640
Who's he?

493
00:23:53,723 --> 00:23:56,017
Uh... 'S my choom D.

494
00:23:56,518 --> 00:23:58,645
D, this is Talia.

495
00:23:58,728 --> 00:24:00,188
What's up?

496
00:24:00,272 --> 00:24:01,773
And, uh, this is Weak.

497
00:24:01,857 --> 00:24:04,151
He's my mom's friend, I guess.

498
00:24:06,528 --> 00:24:08,238
Hmm. Hmm.

499
00:24:08,321 --> 00:24:10,407
You gotta be kidding! It's this one?

500
00:24:10,490 --> 00:24:12,951
- Yep.
- But he's just a kid.

501
00:24:13,034 --> 00:24:15,787
No! He's my boyfriend.

502
00:24:15,871 --> 00:24:18,790
So wipe that stupid grin
off your face and stop being an asshole!

503
00:24:19,958 --> 00:24:22,294
- That's pretty rude, old man.
- See?

504
00:24:22,377 --> 00:24:23,670
This choom gets it.

505
00:24:25,672 --> 00:24:27,007
Oh!

506
00:24:27,966 --> 00:24:29,509
D!

507
00:24:35,348 --> 00:24:39,269
See me, don'tcha? I know you can!

508
00:24:44,024 --> 00:24:45,275
Finally!

509
00:24:46,318 --> 00:24:48,153
I found you!

510
00:25:03,418 --> 00:25:06,171
Didn't mean to sound arrogant

511
00:25:06,254 --> 00:25:10,634
Suddenly we don't feel the same

512
00:25:10,717 --> 00:25:13,178
All I needed was to get it straight

513
00:25:13,261 --> 00:25:17,766
How I feel isn't complicated

514
00:25:17,849 --> 00:25:20,477
Everything that I long to be

515
00:25:20,560 --> 00:25:22,270
You and me

516
00:25:22,354 --> 00:25:24,898
There's more than meets the eye

517
00:25:24,981 --> 00:25:27,817
Everything that I long to be

518
00:25:27,901 --> 00:25:31,530
As in you and

519
00:25:31,613 --> 00:25:38,578
I'm wandering on the city harbour

520
00:25:38,662 --> 00:25:43,375
Now possibly I will see you

521
00:25:43,458 --> 00:25:45,627
In Watson

522
00:25:45,710 --> 00:25:48,338
Run away with me

523
00:25:48,421 --> 00:25:52,759
You're my West Coast problem

524
00:25:52,842 --> 00:25:55,262
